). We attempted removal of the tumor combined with SSS resection because obstruction of the SSS caused by the developed tumor was confirmed. The tumor was consequently removed as Simpson grade II. The residual tumor, including the dural tail sign, was not observed on postoperative magnetic resonance imaging (
). The third histopathological result showed an atypical meningioma, World Health Organization (WHO) grade II. Postoperatively the patient was transferred to a rehabilitation hospital.
